Feature: Agent operations over guest sessions and remote sessions

  @AC-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: Many operations on one lease use one guest session
    Given a running lease whose guest link is "ssh-session"
    When the agent sends 20 execs, 5 pushes and 5 pulls
    Then every request succeeds
    And vm-service ran exactly three channel commands for them: the start that finds no agent, the agent upload, and the start of the one guest session

  @AC-2 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario Outline: Guest operations over a guest session match the ssh link
    Given two leases of one image, one on guest link "ssh" and one on "ssh-session"
    When the agent sends <request> to both
    Then both answers have the same status, "rc" and "output"

    Examples:
      | request                                        |
      | argv ["echo", "a b", "$HOME"]                  |
      | argv ["sh", "-c", "exit 7"]                    |
      | argv ["no-such-command"]                       |
      | script "id -un; echo $PATH; echo err >&2"      |
      | argv ["sleep", "5"] with timeout 1             |
      | push of a host directory, then cat of a file   |
      | pull of a guest file                           |

  @AC-3 @TL-1 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario: Transferred bytes arrive intact or the request fails
    Given a running lease on guest link "ssh-session"
    When the agent pushes a 64 MiB random file and pulls it back
    Then the pulled file has the pushed file's SHA-256
    When one byte of the session stream is changed in transit
    Then the request fails with a corruption error
    And no partial file exists at the destination path

  @AC-4 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A guest session lost during an exec reports uncertain and never reruns it
    Given a running lease on guest link "ssh-session"
    When the agent sends an exec that appends one line to a marker file and then sleeps
    And the guest session's connection is killed while the command runs
    Then the request fails with outcome "uncertain"
    And the marker file has exactly one line
    And the next exec opens a new guest session and succeeds

  @AC-5 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A guest session lost during a read is retried once
    Given a running lease on guest link "ssh-session"
    When the guest session's connection is killed during a pull
    Then vm-service opens a new guest session, reads the file again and the pull succeeds

  @AC-19 @TL-1 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario: A guest session that falls silent fails its request by the silence limit
    Given a running lease on guest link "ssh-session"
    When the agent sends an exec with a timeout of 600 s that appends one line to a marker file
    And nothing arrives from the guest after the exec is sent, though the connection stays open
    Then the request fails with outcome "uncertain" within 5 heartbeat intervals and a margin
    And it is not sent again
    And the next exec opens a new guest session and succeeds
    When the connection stops taking bytes before an exec is fully sent
    Then vm-service ends the channel within the same limit and runs the exec once on a new guest session

  @AC-6 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A remote session resumes after a reset without running a call twice
    Given a client with a remote session through a fault proxy
    When the client calls an exec that appends one line to a marker file and sleeps 3 s
    And the proxy resets the connection after 1 s
    Then the client reconnects, resumes the session and receives the exec's result once
    And the marker file has exactly one line

  @AC-7 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A repeated execution ID returns the first outcome
    Given a completed exec call with execution ID "e-1"
    When the client sends another exec call with execution ID "e-1" on a new session
    Then vm-service answers with the first call's result
    And the command did not run again

  @AC-8 @TL-2 @TL-3
  Scenario: A silent connection is detected and resumed
    Given a client with a remote session through a fault proxy
    When the proxy stops forwarding in both directions but keeps the connection open
    Then both ends close the connection within 15 s of the last frame
    When the proxy forwards again
    Then the client resumes the session and pending results arrive once

  @AC-9 @TL-2 @TL-3
  Scenario: A resume from a new address keeps the session
    Given a client with a remote session and an exec in flight
    When the connection breaks and the client reconnects from a new source port or address
    Then vm-service resumes the same session
    And the exec's result arrives once

  @AC-10 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: An expired session leaves outcomes queryable
    Given a remote session with a grace period of 2 s and an exec in flight
    When the client stays disconnected for 3 s and then resumes
    Then vm-service answers "expired"
    When the client opens a new session and queries the exec's execution ID
    Then the answer is "completed" with the result, or "running"
    And the command ran once

  @AC-11 @TL-3
  Scenario: The remote session passes an HTTPS-only proxy
    Given a client whose only route is an HTTP proxy that allows CONNECT to port 443
    And vm-service's remote session listener on port 443 with TLS
    When the client opens a remote session through the proxy
    Then exec, write and read calls succeed

Feature: Leasing and working on durable machines

  @AC-20 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: A durable machine is acquired by name
    Given an instance with durable exposure on, whose durable machine is "available"
    When the agent posts /acquire with machine set to the durable machine's name and purpose "metal-check"
    Then the response is the machine record with kind "durable", a new lease_id and a workspace path
    And the workspace exists and is empty
    And the machine's state is "leased"
    When the agent posts /acquire with both machine and image
    Then the request is refused with HTTP 400 and nothing is reserved
    When the agent posts /acquire with machine and cpu set
    Then the request is refused with HTTP 400 naming cpu

  @AC-21 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: A durable machine admits one lease at a time, across instances
    Given a durable lease held through one instance with durable exposure on
    When another instance on the same Mac, with its own state directory and exposure on, is asked to acquire the durable machine
    Then it refuses with HTTP 409 and "durable machine leased" naming the purpose and the expiry time
    And the first lease is unchanged

  @AC-22 @TL-2
  Scenario: An operation with a stale lease_id is refused
    Given a durable lease "A" that was released
    And a new durable lease "B" on the same machine
    When the agent sends an exec with lease "A"'s lease_id
    Then the request is refused with HTTP 409 and no command runs
    When the agent sends an exec without a lease_id
    Then the request is refused with HTTP 409 and no command runs

  @AC-23 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: A command runs as wezzard in the GUI session, without the owner's credentials
    Given a durable lease acquired with env "default"
    And the owner's login environment defines ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN and OPENAI_API_KEY
    When the agent runs "id -un; echo $PATH; env | cut -d= -f1; pwd"
    Then the user is "wezzard"
    And PATH contains "/opt/homebrew/bin"
    And the variable names include MACHINE_SERVICE_LEASE_ID, MACHINE_SERVICE_WORKSPACE and TMPDIR
    And the variable names include neither ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN nor OPENAI_API_KEY
    And the working directory is the workspace's "work" folder
    And the command's responsible process for privacy permissions is the machine-service executable, not sshd

  @AC-24 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: Claude Code reaches the gateway with the machine's key
    Given "~/.config/machine-service/agents/claude-code.env" holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, with mode 600 in a mode 700 folder
    And "endpoints.json" beside it names the claude-code base URL "http://<gateway-host>"
    When a durable lease is acquired with env "default"
    Then a command sees ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL equal to "http://<gateway-host>"
    And a command sees ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set
    And a command does not see ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN or CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
    And "claude -p 'reply ok'" answers through the gateway, which attributes the request to this machine's Claude Code key
    When a durable lease is acquired with env "none"
    Then a command sees neither ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL nor ANTHROPIC_API_KEY

  @AC-25 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: Codex reaches the gateway through a per-session custom provider
    Given "~/.config/machine-service/agents/codex.env" holds LITELLM_CODEX_KEY
    And "endpoints.json" names the codex base URL "http://<gateway-host>/v1"
    When a durable lease is acquired with env "default"
    Then CODEX_HOME is the workspace's "codex" folder
    And its config.toml selects a model provider whose base_url is "http://<gateway-host>/v1", as written in endpoints.json, and whose env_key is LITELLM_CODEX_KEY
    And no file in the workspace contains the key's value
    And "~/.codex/config.toml" is unchanged
    And "codex exec" with a model named on its command line answers through the gateway

  @AC-26 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A key is never printed, logged or returned
    Given a durable lease with both agent keys loaded
    When the agent runs "echo $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY $LITELLM_CODEX_KEY"
    Then the exec output contains "[redacted]" twice and neither key's value
    And neither key's value appears in the lease record, the service log, GET /machines, the release report or any error

  @AC-27 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: An unsafe or missing key file is reported, not loaded, and never refuses
    Given "codex.env" has mode 644 and "claude-code.env" is absent
    When the agent lists the machines
    Then the durable machine's agents capability reports codex "unsafe-mode" and claude_code "absent"
    When the agent acquires the durable machine with env "default"
    Then the acquisition succeeds and neither key is loaded

  @AC-28 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: Push and pull to an instance on another Mac carry the bytes
    Given a lease on a machine owned by an instance that is not on loopback
    When the CLI pushes a 64 MiB random file and a directory of 100 files, and pulls both back
    Then each request carries the body's SHA-256 in X-Content-SHA256
    And the pulled bytes match the pushed bytes
    When one byte of a push body is changed in transit
    Then the push fails with a digest mismatch and no file exists at the destination path

  @AC-29 @TL-2 @TL-6
  Scenario: A machine is chosen by capability
    Given instances whose machines are a macOS 26 virtual machine offer, a durable machine with Metal 3 whose CI runner is busy, and a durable machine with Metal 3 whose CI runner is idle
    When the agent runs "machctl acquire --purpose unreal-pp --require metal3"
    Then the CLI prints that it chose the durable machine whose CI runner is idle, and why
    And the virtual machine offer is not chosen, because its gpu reports metal3 false with families mac2 and common3

  @AC-44 @TL-1 @TL-2
  Scenario: A key without a configured endpoint is not loaded
    Given "claude-code.env" holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
    And "endpoints.json" is absent
    When the agent lists the machines
    Then the durable machine's agents capability reports claude_code with key "present" and endpoint "absent"
    When the agent acquires the durable machine with env "default"
    Then the acquisition succeeds
    And a command sees neither ANTHROPIC_API_KEY nor ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
    And no source file, default or document of the service names a gateway host
